1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:03,425
Your graphics card might have 12 gigabytes of memory.

2
00:00:03,705 --> 00:00:09,595
Without one setting, your processor reaches just 256 megabytes of it at a time.

3
00:00:10,945 --> 00:00:14,659
That window is a leftover from 32-bit computers.

4
00:00:14,939 --> 00:00:18,307
To reach the rest, the CPU keeps sliding it along.

5
00:00:19,057 --> 00:00:22,832
Resizable BAR opens the window to the whole card.

6
00:00:23,112 --> 00:00:25,341
Textures and game data go straight in.

7
00:00:26,091 --> 00:00:28,695
Nvidia and AMD cards gain a little.

8
00:00:28,975 --> 00:00:31,239
Intel Arc cards are built around it.

9
00:00:31,519 --> 00:00:38,646
With it off, TechPowerUp's Arc A770 ran almost a quarter slower at 1080p.

10
00:00:39,396 --> 00:00:41,710
So check your BIOS before buying Arc.

11
00:00:41,990 --> 00:00:44,259
If your board can't turn it on, skip Arc.

12
00:00:45,009 --> 00:00:48,026
But is Intel even the right budget pick this year?

13
00:00:48,306 --> 00:00:50,329
The full ranking is linked below.

14
00:00:50,609 --> 00:00:53,406
